# Client Desk environment variables.
# Copy to app/.env.local for local development. Never commit real values.
# Values marked "GitHub secret" go in the repository's Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions, not in any file.

# --- Browser (safe to expose; Row Level Security protects the data) ---
# Supabase → Project Settings → API → Project URL. Used from Phase 1.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# Supabase → Project Settings → API Keys → Publishable key (starts with sb_publishable_). Used from Phase 1.
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxx

# --- GitHub Actions variables (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables) ---
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID        The Firebase project ID, e.g. client-desk-sr. Turns on deploys.

# --- GitHub Actions secrets (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Secrets) ---
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT   The JSON key of the deploy-only service account (see docs/SETUP.md, step 2).
# SUPABASE_DB_URL            Supabase "Session pooler" connection string, with the database password. Backups only.
# SUPABASE_URL               Same as VITE_SUPABASE_URL. Used by the daily keep-alive.
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   Same as VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY. Used by the daily keep-alive.
# BACKUP_PASSPHRASE          A long passphrase that encrypts each backup. Keep a copy in your password manager.
# RCLONE_CONFIG              The contents of rclone.conf for your Google Drive remote named "gdrive".

# --- Server only, never in the browser or this file (Supabase Edge Function secrets, from Phase 1) ---
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY        Supabase secret key (starts with sb_secret_).
# RESEND_API_KEY             Resend API key for sign-in links and digests.
